<h2>Electrical Components Information</h2>

<h3>1. Resistor</h3>
<p>Resistor limits the flow of electric current.</p>

<h3>2. Capacitor</h3>
<p>Capacitor stores electrical energy in an electric field.</p>

<h3>3. Inductor</h3>
<p>Inductor stores energy in a magnetic field.</p>

<h3>4. Diode</h3>
<p>Diode allows current to flow mainly in one direction.</p>

<h3>5. Transformer</h3>
<p>Transformer increases or decreases AC voltage.</p>

<h3>6. Transistor</h3>
<p>Transistor is used for switching and amplification.</p>

